WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:06.420
From the horrifying truth about how Gilbert
made his black flame candles to hidden secrets

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.690
about the Witch Mother, there are some outrageously
plausible Hocus Pocus 2 fan theories we need

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.690
to talk about!

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.830
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and I've
been reading all your comments to find the

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:22.050
very best theories about the Hocus Pocus sequel
and what that ending might really mean!

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:27.380
In Hocus Pocus 2, Gilbert's ultimately responsible
for bringing the Sanderson Sisters back as

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.820
he secretly gives Becca a Black Flame candle
to light on her sixteenth birthday.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.020
And one of our amazing movie lovers, "That_momster_life",
has a particularly gruesome theory about how

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.350
Gilbert made the candle, based on what we
know from the first movie about the grisly

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.610
way those candles are created.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.960
Black Flame Candle.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.770
Made from the fat of a hanged man.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:54.510
Now, public hangings stopped long before Gilbert's
time, but was he so obsessed with the Sanderson

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.329
sisters that he killed someone to make the
black flame candle that would reanimate them?

00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:00.610
They were ahead of their time and they were
misunderstood.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:05.719
In fact, it was Book that taught him the shocking
method he needed to make the magic candle

00:01:05.719 --> 00:01:07.710
on the night the sisters died in 1993.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.159
He showed me how to make another candle.

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:11.689
I mean, it wasn't pretty.

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:15.689
Which means when young Gilbert went to the
witches' cottage he would have discovered

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:20.869
Jay and Ice still locked in their cages as
we saw in the original movie's mid-credits

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:21.869
scene.

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:25.990
Those two bullies who were literally hanging
there could have been the source – the fat

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:30.909
of two hanged men – for the two black flame
candles we know Gilbert made.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:35.959
Terrible as they were though, that would be
an especially brutal form of revenge for stealing

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:37.320
his Halloween candy.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:43.200
So, perhaps Gilbert did his own horrifying,
DIY version of 'liposuction' on the bullies

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.539
instead?!

00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:49.180
The opening scene with the Witch Mother and
the young Sanderson Sisters added some intriguing

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.259
mythology to the Hocus Pocus lore.

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:56.520
It also opened up lots of new questions, such
as what happened to the Witch Mother's coven?

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.700
Where is thy coven?

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.810
Long gone I'm afraid.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.100
The world is not too fond of witches.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.810
At first sight, it seems like she lost her
coven to witch hunters or trials.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.570
However, there are some big clues that she
could well have lost them after casting the

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:16.440
Magicae Maxima spell herself which is why
she warned Winifred against using it, as fellow

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.350
movie lover David points out:
Magicae Maxima makes a witch all-powerful.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.890
It is most frowned upon.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.060
Doomed is the witch that uses this spell.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:30.170
And that theory's supported by "WolfyGirl"
and "EJAM Music"'s observation that the Witch

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:35.670
Mother's eyes glow purple when she uses her
powers, similar to how Winnie's eyes also

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:41.080
go purple as she casts the Magicae Maxima
spell and takes on the extra powers.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.520
All of which makes me wonder if the Witch
Mother originally cast the spell to increase

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.770
her power in order to protect herself and
her coven, but inadvertently lost her sisters

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.770
in the process.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.680
Thou art lucky to have each other.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.830
A witch is nothing without her coven.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:02.260
Hocus Pocus 2 ends with Sarah and Mary first
fading into sparkly dust, Winnie joining them,

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:08.130
and as they merge into a giant swirl of lights,
they disappear with a sudden burst of energy,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.680
seemingly for good this time.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.820
But another of our marvellous movie lovers,
Stephanie, thinks the very final scene of

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:20.100
Becca, Izzy and Cassie doing the iconic Sanderson
witch walk might imply "the original sisters

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.470
have [now] possessed the bodies of the teenage
girls".

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:28.510
And there is a nod towards that idea when
Cassie and Becca say they don't understand

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.610
what's happening to them.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.310
Guys, what are we doing?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.340
I don't know.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:37.230
This could suggest the girls are under the
control or influence of some unknown force.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:42.440
My feeling is this probably isn't the actual
Sanderson sisters reincarnated, but instead

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.500
the mischievous spirit of the infamous trio
has passed on to the new young witches.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.810
It might also have something to do with the
Witch Mother raven which is flying along and

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.430
watching them in that final shot.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:58.240
After the young Sanderson sisters receive
the book from the Witch Mother, the first

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.180
spell they talk about performing is one that
turns a person into a cat.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.570
That would be good to do to John Pritchett.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:10.030
There is a black cat called Cobweb in the
sequel, and movie lover "SaGeForReal" points

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:15.030
out that although we know it isn't Thackery
Binx, the fact that the witches think it is

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.030
Binx...

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.620
I know 'tis really thee, Thackery.
...could suggest they sensed a human spirit

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:26.060
in the cat, which might be that of John Pritchett,
the boy Reverend Traske tried to force young

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.370
Winnie to marry.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.900
It wouldn't surprise me if young Winnie did
punish him, especially given his mean comments

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:33.570
about her in front of the whole village.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:37.240
It is only she is so ugly and unpleasant.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:42.680
In the present day, Cobweb also helps Becca
and Izzy find Book after they escape from

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:47.680
the basement, perhaps because if he is John
Pritchett, he'd want revenge on Winnie and

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.990
her sisters for what they did to him.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:54.851
That reminds me of how after Thackery Binx
was turned into a cat, he helped Max, Allison

00:04:54.851 --> 00:04:56.840
and Dani defeat the witches.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.560
The main issue I can see with this theory
is that we never see Cobweb talking, unlike

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.650
Binx who could speak in the first movie.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:04.790
You can talk.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:05.940
Yeah, no kidding.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.170
Now, get the spell book.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.460
Though that could be addressed in a second
sequel.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.250
Except for the OG witches, a good deal of
the original cast weren't in the sequel, but

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:19.150
it hasn't stopped fans speculating about hidden
references and possibilities.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:24.240
Movie lover "Jessi" says that Cassie's house
looks exactly like Allison's one from the

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.030
first film;
and "anie" also adds that Allison is Cassie's

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:31.790
mother, because according to the actress who
plays Cassie, her cardigan is a deliberate

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.540
call back to Allison's look.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.550
Now, I've checked the houses from each film,
and Cassie's home does have some similar features

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:43.450
to Allison's, such as stairs leading up to
the front door, each house being five-windows

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.450
wide and having shutters.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:50.650
However, Cassie's house is larger, with three
floors below the roof rather than two, and

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.210
there's an additional balcony above the main
entrance.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:59.480
These differences could be explained by assuming
that since 1993 the house has been remodelled

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:00.620
and extended.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:05.080
The main issue with this theory is that Mayor
Traske's campaign poster has both Cassie and

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.919
a woman I assume is her mum in the picture.

00:06:07.919 --> 00:06:13.210
This clearly isn't the grown up Vinessa Shaw
who played Allison, so for the theory to work

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.139
this would have to be Cassie's stepmother,
say.

00:06:16.139 --> 00:06:20.710
Of course, the theory also means Allison and
Max broke up sometime after the end of the

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.129
first movie.

00:06:22.129 --> 00:06:27.389
Regarding the OG gang of Max, Allison and
Dani, a lot of our movie lovers including

00:06:27.389 --> 00:06:32.460
"Veronica" and "thelco" have been speculating
that they could return for a potential third

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.270
movie, perhaps teaming up with the new witch
trio against the Mother Witch who would be

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.740
the new villain;
which could be an awful lot of fun!

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:46.010
Additionally, a likely plot for a third movie
would be a prequel story involving the three

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.120
young Sanderson sisters.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:53.190
As Batman's alter ego points out, Bette Midler
has said she was pleased that in Hocus Pocus

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:58.370
2 the filmmakers decided to let Winnie go
at the end, after she realised her family

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:03.330
was the most important thing to her, and Midler
thinks the three sisters should be laid to

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.230
rest now, rather that returning for another
movie.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:10.940
"Bruce Wayne" goes on to say that a prequel
story could be very interesting if it follows

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:15.639
the young sisters after they're exiled from
Salem, go to live in the Forbidden Forest,

00:07:15.639 --> 00:07:19.770
and shows them interacting with the Mother
Witch and their experiments with Book.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.690
I think that sounds great.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:25.770
The young actresses did a good job and I'm
sure fans would love to see a lot more of

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.949
Hannah Waddingham's Mother Witch.

00:07:27.949 --> 00:07:32.750
And as we already know from her work in the
show Ted Lasso, Waddingham could also easily

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:37.530
do a musical number in the third movie, as
another of our awesome movie lovers "Miranda"

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:38.690
points out.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:43.210
They could even jump into the present day
for some of the story by setting up a connection

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:47.530
between the young Sanderson Sisters and characters
from the first or second movies.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:52.860
For example, fellow movie lover "Roland" suggests
they could have Allison be a descendant of

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.340
Winnie, through her relationship with Billy.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:08:00.250
This overall idea of Winnie being Allison's
ancestor could work, though I don't think

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.940
it would be with Billy as he insisted in the
second movie that he only shared a single

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:05.979
kiss with Winifred.

00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:10.860
By the way, Roland's theory about Winnie and
Allison being related would also fit with

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:14.820
the popular fan theory about Allison being
a secret witch!

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.380
So, what do you think about these Hocus Pocus
2 theories?

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.580
And what would you like to see in a potential
third movie?

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:26.790
Next, tap left to discover all the easter
eggs and little details I spotted in the sequel.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.860
And if you enjoyed this video, do leave a
thumbs-up, I really appreciate it.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:35.659
Thanks for enjoying this movie with me and
hope you have a marvellous movie-loving week!

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:37.080
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

